{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Fixed — Gerrit change 1427\n\n**Root cause (re-verified, not re-derived).** Gerrit's Verified lane takes the workflow\nDEFINITION from the target branch but checks out the CHANGE'S tree, so a gate step added on\nmain runs against open changes whose base predates its script. Reproduced directly: running\n`python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py` and `python scripts/check_config_reads.py` in a\ndirectory without them exits **2** with `can't open file ... [Errno 2]` — a hard CI failure\nindistinguishable from a real gate violation.\n\n**Guarded — 11 steps, exactly the set this ticket enumerated.**\n\n`_build-and-test.yml` (9): Verified-gate parity, comment-hygiene, Env-var registry drift,\nDocs-index completeness, README quickstart golden-path, CLI-reference drift, MCP-reference\ndrift, server.json env-contract drift, Config-read.\n\n`gerrit-verify.yaml` golden-path (2): README quickstart golden-path, End-to-end CLI probe.\n\nEach gains the same early-return guard the raw-git-write gate uses. **Everything below each\nguard is byte-for-byte unchanged.** The only deletions in the whole diff are five inline\n`run:` lines becoming block form, with their command preserved verbatim — a reviewer can\nconfirm no gate was weakened by reading the deletion list alone.\n\n**Both tree cases proven per step** (`tests/unit/test_gate_step_tree_skew.py`, which lifts\neach step's real `run:` body out of the live YAML and executes it under the shell GitHub\nActions would use):\n\n- *absent script* — exit 0, a log line naming the tree-skew cause, no `::error::` annotation;\n- *present script* — a stub that records that it ran and then exits non-zero: the step must\n  both invoke it and still fail the build. Enforcement intact.\n\n**RED to GREEN.** 33 failures before the fix (11 structural + 22 behavioral), 53 passed after.\nMutation-checked in both directions: removing one guard returns its 3 tests to RED; making a\nguard always-skip returns the present-script test to RED, so the tests catch weakening too.\n\n**The structural guard landed.** It walks both patchset-lane workflows, selects only the jobs\nthat use `checkout-gerrit-change-action` (the ones that check out the change's tree), and\nfails on any step running a repo script without an if-present guard. The ee2a convention no\nlonger depends on an author remembering the note — this prevents the 12th instance, not just\nthe 11. Scoping needed no design decision: the vote job's `normalize_ci_conclusion` step is\ncorrectly excluded because it deliberately sparse-checks-out its script from the trusted\ndefault branch, not the patchset. A vacuity assertion guards the detector itself.\n\n**Scope and safety.** No new dependency, no pre-existing test touched, no enforcement path\naltered. Full unit suite 3923 passed / 0 failed; lint + mypy clean; zizmor findings identical\npre- and post-change (22, none new); actionlint clean.\n\nNot closing until Verified +1 and merged."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785915227537625001,"uuid":"8cce446a-3f60-43ef-aa23-1dd341d8e572"}